From: Jacob Riff <jacob@riff.dk>
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] platform/x86: int3472: Map power enable to "vana" for VD55G1 (TBE20A1)

The vd55g1 driver requests its supplies as "vcore"/"vddio"/"vana". On
the Lenovo ThinkPad X1 Carbon Gen 14 the IR camera module has a single
INT3472-managed power-enable GPIO; map it to "vana" so the driver's
regulator_bulk_enable() actually powers the sensor (same pattern as the
IMX471 entries for SONY471A/TBE20A0). Without this the rail maps to a
dummy regulator and probing fails.

Tested-on: Lenovo ThinkPad X1 Carbon Gen 14 21V7CTO1WW, kernel 7.1.4
Signed-off-by: Jacob Riff <jacob@riff.dk>
---
--- a/drivers/platform/x86/intel/int3472/discrete.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/intel/int3472/discrete.c
@@ -182,6 +182,13 @@
 		.con_id = "vana",
 		.enable_time_us = GPIO_REGULATOR_ENABLE_TIME,
 	},
+	{	/* vd55g1 IR cam (Lenovo X1 Carbon G14): power enable -> "vana" */
+		.hid = "TBE20A1",
+		.type_from = INT3472_GPIO_TYPE_POWER_ENABLE,
+		.type_to = INT3472_GPIO_TYPE_POWER_ENABLE,
+		.con_id = "vana",
+		.enable_time_us = GPIO_REGULATOR_ENABLE_TIME,
+	},
 };
 
 static void int3472_get_con_id_and_polarity(struct int3472_discrete_device *int3472, u8 *type,
